{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-mass-identity-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:mass-identity-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the inertial mass identity","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-identity"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-mass-identity-exists"],"tags":["existence","mass-identity","inertial-mass"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.MassIdentity.exists","text":"mass-identity-exists.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:mass-identity-exists\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe (<a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\">quantum observable universe</a>) and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A</code> a closed cycle. The inertial mass</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathfrak{m}(\\varrho)\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\bigl\\lVert\n    \\mathrm{tr}\\bigl( (\\int_A \\otimes \\mathrm{id}) \\circ \\Delta \\circ \\varrho \\bigr)\n  \\bigr\\rVert</code></pre>\n<p>(<a href=\"#def:mass-identity\">mass identity</a>) exists as a well-defined element of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> for every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho</code>. We prove uniqueness in <a href=\"#prop:mass-identity-unique\">uniqueness of the mass identity</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-exists.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"8.1.3"}
